Resolved / settled work is summarised here in one or two lines only. The full  
reasoning, derivations, part numbers and history live in project-long.txt in  
the same sys folder (Drive ID: __FILL IN AFTER UPLOAD__). Fetch that file only  
when the summary here is genuinely insufficient — it is ~70KB and expensive to  
pull for no reason.  

SESSION BOOTSTRAP  
1. Read this file (project.txt, ID 1D93u56_lanbWWxL06J5bvLS5Emb5yV4M)  
2. Work from this file. Fetch project-long.txt only for detail not held here.  
3. Config files: search sys folder 1gLAcXXCszW8oZrBpZwaeeRTaJNPs9gTI or  
   macros folder 1oXYyhdUJHUqfROvr4jJeL3fo5T1uOwUI by filename  
4. config.g on Drive is AUTHORITATIVE for firmware settings. Both project files  
   are secondary and lag verbal session decisions — cross-check, don't assume.  
5. Drive is the live source. Do NOT fetch from GitHub raw URLs.  
6. Check gcodes.txt before issuing any GCode command.  

WORKING STYLE  
- Direct, technically precise. No hand-holding. One step at a time.  
- Changed blocks, not full file dumps, unless asked.  
- Hardware fixes preferred over software workarounds.  
- Verify against the physical part or the manufacturer's datasheet — never  
  convention, forum posts, or prior AI output. This has caught real errors  
  repeatedly (pump variant, M569 D-parameter, CPAP hose OD, X beam wall).  
- When a documented value and a physical observation disagree, the observation  
  wins.  
- Settle design questions to a firm decision before writing code or config.  
- Own errors precisely and correct immediately. Do not deflect.  
- Do not re-raise anything under DO NOT REOPEN.  

FILE UPDATES — CRITICAL  
Claude NEVER writes, creates or uploads any file, to Drive or anywhere else.  
Output plain-text diffs or replacement blocks only; Trev uploads manually.  
NEVER regenerate either project file in full from context — patch by anchored  
find/replace against a fresh fetch.  

RRF QUIRK: daemon.g cannot be edited in place while RRF is running it. Rename  
(e.g. daem6on.g), edit, rename back.  

=======================================================================================================  
MACHINE AT A GLANCE  
=======================================================================================================  
415 x 415 x 440mm CoreXY AWD HevORT. Duet 3 6HC v1.02c, SBC mode, Pi 4  
(hostname hevort, user trev). RRF 3.7.0-beta.3 as of 20/08/2026.  

Motion   : 4x M23CL-76-2804 CAN-FD on 48V via TDB v1.0. D4 closed loop, tuned.  
           CAN 70 = X1 back-right, 71 = X2 front-left,  
           CAN 72 = Y1 front-right, 73 = Y2 back-left.  
           12mm 2GT Gates EPDM belts, Mellow CNC EvoHevORT towers.  
           X beam 20x20x3mm aluminium, single MGN9 rail.  
Z        : 3x 42HSB47A41505 brake steppers, drivers 0.0/0.1/0.2, brakes OUT1.  
           Z0=front-left arm, Z1=rear arm, Z2=front-right arm (M671 order).  
Toolhead : Goliath water-cooled + VZ-HextrudORT Low Plus (12mm bore).  
           Mellow ALPS strain-gauge Z probe on IO6. WS7040 CPAP part cooling.  
Bed      : 440x440x20mm granite + 4mm FR4, 400x400mm 1400W polyimide mat.  
Chamber  : 1400W PTC, Siemens S7-1212C PLC (FW V4.3.1), cascade PID,  
           Modbus RTU to Duet on IO1 (M575 P3 B9600 S7).  
Network  : PROFINET 192.168.32.x — Pi .70, PLC .71, KTP700 .72, switch .73.  

