---------------------------------------------------------------------------  
5. global.awdDriveMode — REDESIGN OUTSTANDING  
---------------------------------------------------------------------------  
Purpose: switch AWD drive mode from a DWC macro without hand-editing config.  

First pass (REJECTED, do not implement as drafted): global.awdClosedLoop as a  
0/1 boolean, with matching if/else blocks in the restore-mode section of  
homex.g, homey.g and homeall.g, plus new sys/closedloop.g and sys/openloop.g  
macros that flip the variable and trigger G28 X Y.  

REQUIRED INSTEAD: the variable stores the ACTUAL D value (2 / 4 / 5) directly,  
not a boolean, so any mode is selectable from one variable. Redesign not yet  
done.  

Relevant constraint: M569.1 issued WITH parameters drops drivers from D4 to D2  
(open loop), so a re-home is required to restore closed loop. This is why the  
mode restore lives in the homing files at all.  

---------------------------------------------------------------------------  
6. INPUT SHAPING / VIBRATION  [in progress]  
---------------------------------------------------------------------------  
Done so far: ~127 Hz structural gantry mode treated with M593 P"zvd" F127,  
which halved X ring-down rms.  

Remaining, in priority order:  

 a. ~215 Hz mode — CONFIRMED as the first torsional mode of the X beam  
    (20x20x3mm 6063 aluminium, single MGN9 rail). Excited by Y acceleration  
    acting through the toolhead CoM offset below the beam shear centre.  
    Antinode at mid-span, confirmed by a three-position X test.  
    Two fixes, both hardware:  
      - Reduce the toolhead CoM vertical offset below the beam axis.  
      - Constrained-layer damping tape inside the tube.  
    Shaping alone will not remove this; it is a stiffness/geometry problem.  

 b. ~312 Hz mode — local to the hotend mount. The ALPS strain gauge  
    Z-compliance flexure is a likely contributor; the hotend is perceptibly  
    wobbly by hand. Stiffen the mount.  

 c. Velocity ceiling is ~600-700 mm/s (audible resonance, loop saturates).  
    Raising it depends on (a) and (b). Once resolved, raise M201/M203 from  
    their current placeholders.  

MEASUREMENT DISCIPLINE — this has bitten before:  
 - Single accelerometer captures have ~15% run-to-run scatter. Do at least  
   THREE runs before trusting any modest effect.  
 - Velocity sweeps distinguish structural modes (frequency does not scale with  
   velocity) from forced modes (belt tooth-passing, bearing ball-pass).  
 - Sensor relocation amplitude ratio confirms rotation axis and mode shape  
   geometrically.  
 - Run macros/accel_setup.g manually before a session — the accelerometer  
   config is deliberately NOT in config.g.  

